<title>USA: UN SAYS TWO IRAQI OIL CONTRACTS OKAYED, TOTAL FIVE.</title>
<headline>UN SAYS TWO IRAQI OIL CONTRACTS OKAYED, TOTAL FIVE.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.N. overseers have approved two more Iraqi oil contracts, bringing the total number to five since the second round &quot;oil-for-food&quot; sales resumed on Friday, according to U.N. spokesman Hiro Ueki Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The fourth contract was for 13.5 million barrels and the fifth for 3.6 million barrels,&quot; said Ueki.</p>
<p>The total barrel count for the five approved contracts now stands at 31.42 million barrels, according to U.N. tabulations, though officials would not reveal the time period for the contracts.</p>
<p>Ueki noted that 17 contracts have thus far been received by overseers, who have 24 hours to consider completed contract proposals.</p>
<p>((--Patrick Connole, NY Oil Desk, +1 212 859 1828))</p>
</text>
